            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 12 changed paths. The change adds a goal check to the longterm-mem query gate. It applies only under scope goal, and only after the project check.",
              "The goal argument is decoded the same way project is. A missing, null, non-string or empty goal becomes an empty string, which is denied under scope goal. A different goal is also denied. This tightens enforcement and does not widen access.",
              "If a goal-scoped plan has an empty goal, the gate allows the query with a warning. This is fail-open. It is unreachable through Resolve, as the code comment and a test state, and it matches the existing handling of a plan with no project. I treated it as hypothetical, not as a reachable exploit.",
              "Denial messages pass the plan's goal and project through sanitizeLine, and the caller-supplied goal through quoteValue. I saw no injection or data exposure in the new reason strings.",
              "No dependency, secret or lockfile changes. The change adds no new I/O and no new input parsing beyond one extra JSON string field.",
              "Under scope project the goal argument is deliberately unchecked. This is the requested behavior and the tests document it. Baseline behavior is unchanged for that case."
            ]
          }
        }
