              {
                "id": "R3-goal-sanitize-nonempty",
                "lens": "reliability",
                "location": "engine/projection/gate.go:497-503",
                "severity": "SUGGESTION",
                "claim": "The goal denial reasons are built from the model-supplied goal via quoteValue and from the plan goal via sanitizeLine. Tests cover case and whitespace differences, but none covers a goal containing control characters or newlines. The sanitization is reused from the project path, so the risk is low.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/projection/gate.go:497-503",
                  "engine/projection/gate_goal_test.go:31-35"
                ]
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "I reviewed all 12 changed paths. The goal is decoded as text, with a missing, null or non-text value becoming empty. It is checked after the project, and only when the scope is goal.",
              "The new tests cover each of these cases: a matching goal, a missing goal, another goal, a goal of the wrong type, and the project check running first. They also cover scope project leaving the goal unchecked, unnamed arguments, and an empty plan goal, which gives a warning instead of a denial. The hookwire decoder, the gateCall translation and an end-to-end hook run are each tested.",
              "I found no regression on input that was valid before this change. The only changed behavior is that a goal-scoped longterm-mem query is now denied unless it names the plan's goal, which is the requested behavior."
